{"node":{"id":"HP:0025373","label":"Interictal EEG abnormality","ic":3.535,"definition":"Interictal refers to a period of time between epileptic seizures. Electroencephalographic (EEG) patterns are important in the differential diagnosis of epilepsy, and the EEG is almost always abnormal during a seizure. Some persons with seizures may show EEG abnormalities between seizures, while others do not. In some cases, multiple interictal EEGs must be recorded before an abnormality is observed. In most cases the electrographic pattern of seizure onset is completely different from the activity recorded during interictal discharge."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0010524","label":"X-linked sideroblastic anemia with ataxia","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_0d95f2f94ddf","source":"MONDO:0010524","target":"HP:0025373","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:301310 · PMID:34354969","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34354969/","level":"observed","date":"2024-04-01","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Anemia, sideroblastic, and spinocerebellar ataxia: Interictal EEG abnormality (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:1060177","label":"developmental and epileptic encephalopathy 119","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_06e18d54fd6d","source":"MONDO:1060177","target":"HP:0025373","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:621304 · PMID:40210679","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40210679/","level":"observed","date":"2025-11-22","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Developmental and epileptic encephalopathy 119: Interictal EEG abnormality (frequency 2/2) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0009509","label":"Landau-Kleffner syndrome","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_dc98207e8700","source":"MONDO:0009509","target":"HP:0025373","type":"has_phen